there are new questions today about why  a North Carolina  teenager who was violently arrested  during what his mother says was a mental  health emergency received a plea deal  instead of the treatment he was seeking  yesterday we showed you video of Hayden  long being tackled to the ground tased  and then punched while in handcuffs  after his mother tried to take him to a  hospital ER Janet shamlian is outside  that hospital in Lincolnton North  Carolina Janet why did the teenager take  the plea Anthony good morning Hayden's  mom Jessica says he took that plea deal  to avoid being tried as an adult on the  felony assault charge now the incident  is raising questions about how people  with potential mental health issues  should be treated and cared for an  expert saying that Hayden should have  been met with help not handcuffs  Hayden long pleaded guilty in juvenile  court Monday to two misdemeanor charges  one for assault the other underage  drinking because the alternative was  letting my sixteen-year-old son go to  court as an adult this was the easiest  and the safest route to take it came  after this incident outside the North  Carolina hospital where his mom had  taken him for help  believing he was having a mental  breakdown security video shows Hayden  spitting blood on deputy Justin Polson  who responded by punching the 16  year-old in the head Hayden was  handcuffed at the time in court Monday  deputy Polson said he was no longer with  the Sheriff's Department it's not known  if he was fired for his actions he  testified he didn't believe the teen  needed mental health treatment at the  time Hayden's mom defended her son's  behavior mental illness displays in a  lot of different ways well maybe he  drank the alcohol because he is mentally  ill he is suffering from something else  and trying to self-medicate the video  showing hospital security guards and  sheriff's deputies responding with force  is alarming to Angela Kimball with the  National Alliance on Mental Illness when  parents take their child to the  emergency department  they're expecting hell  not handcuffs children like Hayden  deserved treatment and safety and he got  neither Kimble says hospitals and first  responders need to know how to  de-escalate these situations trained  mental health professionals know that  people's behaviors can be very agitated  that's one thing we have to recognize  otherwise we end up harming people in  court Hayden told the judge he was  taking antidepressants at the time his  mother says she hopes the incident will  be a wake-up call not just for parents  but also for law enforcement the family  has not decided whether to pursue legal  action Gale who Janet that video is  tough to watch thank you very much  I see the tough spot the mother's into  because she clearly thinks that  behaviors egregious and looking at on  the tape it does seem to be so you also  don't want to put your son like that at  16 yeah very tough spot but taken you  don't feel he's guilty
 

